			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1447352">
									

<p>He still has a point. If this thing is just there, in this room, directly connected to the hallway, what's it going to do the moment that door is opened for any reason?</p>
<p>Also, as this note evinces, there is a reason. The gap gives it access to things for &quot;synthesis.&quot; The possibility can't be ruled out, going by this alone, that it could synthesize the mice and spider together and release this under the door.</p>
<p>And the Foundation needs to hire an exterminator because they have mice in a sterile scientific facility.</p>

